{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-341953",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We have the function \n\n$$\ny=(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))^{′}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)))+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)))}^{′} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡(x))) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,{csc}^{2}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,(\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x)})}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)})} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-y(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x))\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
